  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-27T05:32:23.245Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've noticed that VR chat has you looking down a lot to confirm things rather than looking at eye level.\nIt looks like the biomechanics of VR are just starting to get studied and one of the suggestions is that things should appear at eye level when possible:\nhttps://www.safetyandhealthmagazine.com/articles/19515-reduce-ergonomic-hazards-of-vr-during-design-and-development-researchers-say\nMy request is that an option be added so that menus and in-game UIs appear in a fixed position at nearly eye level in front of you rather than attached to your hands, this would also allow users who can't use both hands to get by with the current controls because the menu is wouldn't be attached to your hands you wouldn't have to use two hands to select things. I personally have lots of carpal tunnel damage and would like to avoid using both hands when I can.",
